--- Overview
Moves config file location out of cmdutil into a new cmdutil/cmdconfig package and adds FilesFlag, a flag that takes multiple YAML, .env and JSON files. Also adds YAML loading, environment-variable expansion and subcmd hooks that load the config and set up logging for commands.

--- Key Changes
cmdutil/cmdconfig (new)
  * Moved and renamed the locate functions: ConfigFilePath -> SearchPath, LocateConfigFilePath -> LocateFilePath, LocateConfigFileInDir -> LocateFile, LocateConfigFilesInDir -> LocateFiles. Added LocateFilesPath.
  * FilesFlag: a repeatable flag that takes comma-separated files and sorts them by suffix into YAML, .env or JSON. Files set on the command line replace the defaults. It supports SetDefault, SetDefaults and DefaultValues.
  * FilesFlag.Locate(Spec) returns a Located:
    * Precedence is flag, then environment variable (Spec.EnvVars), then defaults.
    * Files from the flag or env var must exist; missing defaults are skipped.
    * Spec.FirstOnly returns only the first file found for the listed types.
    * Spec.Path can override the search path.

cmdutil
  * Added generic ContextWithValue / ContextValue[T], which key context values by their type.

cmdutil/cmdyaml
  * Load / LoadFiles: merge the located .env files, then strictly parse the YAML files. $VAR references are expanded from the process environment first, then from the env files.
  * The existing LocateConfig* wrappers now call cmdconfig.

cmdutil/envfile
  * ExpandingMapping: an os.Expand mapping where the environment wins over file variables. References inside file values are expanded recursively, up to a depth limit. Unresolved references stay as ${NAME}.

cmdutil/flags
  * RegisterFlagsInStruct uses a field's DefaultValues() result when the tag has no default.
  * Defaults go to the field's SetDefault(string) error method if it has one, otherwise to Set.

cmdutil/subcmd
  * ConfigHook[T]: a PreHook that loads config through cmdyaml.Load.
    * Optionally requires a YAML file.
    * Calls Validate() on the config if it was read from a file.
    * Errors name the file to edit.
    * Stores the result in the context through Store.
  * LoggerHook: a PreHook that builds a logger from the global flags, adds it to the context and closes it after the command runs.

--- Breaking Changes
  * Removed cmdutil.ConfigFilePath, cmdutil.LocateConfigFilePath, cmdutil.LocateConfigFileInDir and cmdutil.LocateConfigFilesInDir. Use the renamed versions in cloudeng.io/cmdutil/cmdconfig.
  * flags.RegisterFlagsInStruct behaves differently for flag.Value fields that already have a DefaultValues() or SetDefault(string) error method. Those fields now get a default even when the tag leaves it empty, and defaults go to SetDefault instead of Set.

